 "verdict": "Intensive over the full 16x range in clone area (N = 6,144 to 98,304 cells): weighted slope of mu_d*/s_d vs log10(N) = -0.017 per decade, 95% CI [-0.223, +0.188], consistent with 0; all five points are consistent with a single flat value (chi2 = 2.79 on 4 dof, p = 0.59); weighted mean mu_d*/s_d = 0.442 [95% CI 0.400, 0.483]. Bound: the reduced-power N = 98,304 arm limits the excluded drift to |slope| >~ 0.2 per decade. Caveat (aspect control): at fixed N = 49,152 the wide-aspect geometry 384x128 gives mu_d*/s_d = 0.58 [0.48, 0.65] versus 0.39 [0.32, 0.53] at 192x256 (bootstrap difference in mu_d* = +0.0019 [+0.0000, +0.0030], P(diff<=0) = 0.024): the threshold is intensive in clone AREA along the paper's fixed-L_long axis but is not aspect-invariant, so N alone does not fully parameterize it.",
 "data": "intensivity_ext.parquet (this campaign; groups N49k/T3_49k=192x256, N98k/T3_98k=192x512, N49kW/T3_49kW=384x128 control) + prior three points from ridge_law.parquet"
